WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.938
Vendors teach their products,

2
00:00:01.938 --> 00:00:05.412
and the book names them as
examples, never endorsements.

3
00:00:05.412 --> 00:00:08.988
A vendor course earns a place
only if it passes four tests:

4
00:00:08.988 --> 00:00:12.869
it maps to a book procedure; it's
current; the agency can keep its

5
00:00:12.869 --> 00:00:17.662
completion record; and the agency knows
how the vendor handles learner data.

6
00:00:17.662 --> 00:00:21.937
Exam records tied to a work account
are lost when the person leaves,

7
00:00:21.937 --> 00:00:24.113
so the agency keeps its own record.

8
00:00:24.113 --> 00:00:27.700
Lab environments are harder to
get than most programs expect.

9
00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:30.412
Microsoft Learn's free sandboxes are gone.

10
00:00:30.412 --> 00:00:35.135
The developer sandbox has eligibility
limits and isn't offered in any

11
00:00:35.135 --> 00:00:39.288
government cloud, and there's no
free sandbox in G C C High at all.

12
00:00:39.288 --> 00:00:43.237
So the program office arranges lab
tenants, and before each gate the

13
00:00:43.237 --> 00:00:47.538
team rehearses once in the agency's
own non-production government tenant.

14
00:00:47.538 --> 00:00:52.847
Every lab follows the same rules: never
production; emergency access first;

15
00:00:52.847 --> 00:00:57.472
observe before enforcing; no sync
or federation with production;

16
00:00:57.472 --> 00:01:00.790
synthetic data only; and
tear it down at the end.
